Glossary of ALM Terms: 

ALM (Application Lifecycle Management) – End-to-end management of app development from conception to retirement, including governance, dev, and maintenance【27†L18-L26】. 

Environment – Isolated space for Power Platform apps/flows with its own Dataverse; e.g., Dev, Test, Prod【1†L65-L72】. 

Solution – Package of Power Platform components (like apps, flows, tables) for moving customizations between environments【27†L32-L40】. 

Managed Solution – Deployed (imported) solution where components are locked for changes in target; used in non-dev environments【22†L50-L58】. 

Unmanaged Solution – Editable solution used in development, source of truth for modifications【22†L50-L58】. 

Solution Publisher – Metadata about who made a solution; defines unique prefix for components. 

Solution Layer – Representation of an installed solution’s effects on components in layered order (top layer’s changes apply last)【12†L42-L50】. 

Upgrade vs Update – Import actions: Upgrade removes missing components, Update doesn’t remove. 

Environment Variable – Config setting (with default/current values) that travels with solution definitions for environment-specific differences【24†L35-L43】. 

Connection Reference – Solution component linking connectors in apps/flows to an actual environment connection. 

Solution Checker – Analyzer tool scanning solutions for issues and best practice violations before deployment. 

Power Platform Pipelines – In-product ALM pipeline for deploying solutions across environments with low-code approach【13†L14-L22】. 

Azure DevOps/GitHub ALM – Use of DevOps pipelines or GitHub Actions for automating ALM with code-based workflows (includes Power Platform Build Tools). 

Configuration Migration Tool – Tool to export/import reference data across environments (for moving data, not included in solutions)【17†L4-L12】. 

PL-200 – Microsoft Power Platform Functional Consultant exam; covers ALM topics such as solutions, environment strategies, etc., with focus on practical application. 

